Right now I run something like:

rm -f tmp/done && while [ ! -f tmp/done ]; do claude --permission-mode auto -p "/process-email and ${NOTIFY_URL} when done ; if inbox is empty,uch $(jj root)/tmp/done"; done

Add a `just process-email` just task that does the work
deterministically. It should:

1. update the jj mail dir
2. notmuch index
3. check for inbox messages. if there are any, process them one at a time,
oldest first. for each one, notify ${NOTIFY_URL}
4. when there are no inbox messages, exit

NOTIFY_URL will be provided as a secret, similar to how we provide mail
secrets for lab-mail jail.
